  "body": "This week I ran into a possible issue with the way `naturalWidth` and `naturalHeight` is handled on image tags using `srcset`.\n\nAs I understand, `naturalWidth` and `naturalHeight` should return the actual size of the image file.\n\nBut Chrome reports different sizes depending on the space occupied by the tag.\n\nOn http://codepen.io/davidmh/pen/PZooJL/ I'm using and image tag with three different dimensions on the `srcset` using http://placehold.it which prints the real dimensions on the image in it.\n\nThis is Safari mobile reporting the right width and height:\nhttp://i.imgur.com/lAgTmwD.png\n\nChrome does not report the right natural dimensions, this one should be 760x665, but it reports 211x185\nhttp://i.imgur.com/0JtQtKF.png\n\nSwitching into portrait changes the natural dimensions:\nhttp://i.imgur.com/8bwt7CN.png\n\nCan anyone confirm this issue?\n",
